# Painted parts

The sprite is a transparent rectangle equal to the box collider.
`HumanSegment` sets `sprite.size = collider.size` and stretches the
full PNG onto that box (`Sliced`). Empty pixels stay empty: that is
how a short hand sits in `handSize` 0.06 × 0.32. Do not crop
`OpaqueRect`. Do not grow `VisualSize` on painted parts. Do not
change `handSize` / `pawSize` / `footSize` to fix the picture.

A species is one animal. Judge the assembled body in Play, not the
folder of crops.

## Canvas

- Draw the canvas in the **collider aspect** (fields on `Human` /
  `Dog` / `Bird`). Face +X, side view.
- One bone per PNG. No extra neck on the head, no second joint bend
  on a straight bone. Proximal toward the parent joint.
- Prefer one side-view sheet, then split (`ArtIncoming` +
  `Tools/SplitSheet`). A locked reference on every later call is a
  fallback, not a plan.

## Stretch is the mapping

`Sliced` maps the whole canvas onto the collider. If the PNG aspect
does not match the box, the drawing stretches. Match the box; do not
ask the collider to match the PNG.

A padded silhouette with most of the canvas empty will look small
inside the bone. Fill the rectangle, or leave empty space on purpose
(hand in a long box).

Generated capsules (no painted key) still overlap at the hinge
(`VisualSize` 1.18 / 1.26). Painted parts do not.

## The draw mode owns the size, never the transform

Assign the draw mode **before** the picture and the size
(`ArtParts.Dress`: mode, `sprite`, `size`, `color`). Unity keeps the
current world box when a `Simple` renderer is converted to
`Sliced`/`Tiled` and writes it as the transform's `localScale`, so the
old order (picture, `size`, mode) left every tiled part drawn at the
canvas' own natural size: a `bark` limb of 0.10 × 0.30 m with the
0.5 m period came out 0.50 × 0.50 m (scale 5.00 / 1.68), a petal
1.28× / 1.60× its box. Where the canvas aspect equals the box aspect
(the padded human parts, the three logs) the factor is ~1, which is
why the frames looked right. With the mode first the factor is
exactly 1 and the dress writes `sprite` / `size` / `color` only.
Evidence: `Art1Check.ScaleAudit`, the check `dressing moves no
localScale`, `Trials/Runs/art-0-dressorder-21st-report.md`.

## Joints

A hard outline on the cut face becomes a dark seam when two bones
rotate. Leave the cut soft. Do not bake a posed bend that fights
the hinge. Do not close a gap by moving the collider.

## Background

Transparent. Punch only near-white, low chroma. A black studio fill
stays as an opaque slab. Check a corner **and** a pixel beside the
silhouette, not only `A00=0`.

## Done means assembled

Crops in `ArtIncoming/*/gen` are not acceptance. Open the Play scene
of that species (`SampleScene`, `Dog`, `Bird`, `Chicken`). If Unity
is closed, say so — do not call the folder "the dog".
